---
/**
 * Original BotPlanet explainer — how a mower knows where the lawn stops.
 *
 * THE DECISION THIS PAGE EXISTS FOR is buried in three paragraphs of prose:
 * a buried wire you install once and cannot easily change, satellite RTK that
 * needs a clear view of the sky, or on-board vision that needs light and edges
 * it can see. Those are not three grades of the same thing — they fail in
 * completely different places, and the failure is what decides the purchase.
 * A garden under heavy tree cover rules out RTK; a garden with no clean lawn
 * edge is hard for vision; a garden the owner intends to re-landscape is a bad
 * place to bury 200 metres of wire.
 *
 * Drawn as one garden three times so the difference is in the method rather
 * than in the plot. Conceptual: no product is named and no accuracy figure is
 * claimed, because those belong on a review beside the source that gave them.
 */
---
<figure class="dgm">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 300" width="100%" role="img"
    aria-label="The same garden shown three times: bounded by a buried perimeter wire, by satellite RTK positioning, and by on-board camera vision. Each panel names what that method needs and where it fails.">
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="300" rx="14" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--border)"/>

    <text x="24" y="34" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="#f5f5f7">Three ways a mower finds the edge</text>
    <text x="24" y="54" font-size="11.5" fill="#c9c9d1">They fail in different places, which is what decides the choice.</text>

    <!-- 1. buried wire -->
    <g>
      <text x="24" y="86" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#7c93ff">Buried wire</text>
      <rect x="24" y="96" width="176" height="104" rx="8" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--border-2)"/>
      <path d="M40 178 L40 116 L184 116 L184 178 Z" fill="rgba(124,147,255,0.08)" stroke="#7c93ff" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
      <circle cx="112" cy="150" r="9" fill="#7c93ff"/>
      <text x="24" y="222" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">Needs: a day with a spade.</text>
      <text x="24" y="238" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">Fails when: you move a bed,</text>
      <text x="24" y="254" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">or the wire is cut.</text>
      <text x="24" y="276" font-size="11" fill="#8b8b95">Works under trees.</text>
    </g>

    <!-- 2. satellite RTK -->
    <g>
      <text x="232" y="86" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#4fd1c5">Satellite (RTK)</text>
      <rect x="232" y="96" width="176" height="104" rx="8" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--border-2)"/>
      <path d="M248 178 L248 116 L392 116 L392 178 Z" fill="rgba(79,209,197,0.08)" stroke="#4fd1c5" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <circle cx="320" cy="152" r="9" fill="#4fd1c5"/>
      <path d="M320 143 L306 108" stroke="#4fd1c5" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <path d="M320 143 L338 106" stroke="#4fd1c5" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <text x="300" y="104" font-size="12" fill="#4fd1c5">🛰</text>
      <text x="232" y="222" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">Needs: open sky, and an</text>
      <text x="232" y="238" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">aerial with a clear view.</text>
      <text x="232" y="254" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">Fails when: tree cover,</text>
      <text x="232" y="270" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">tall walls, narrow side returns.</text>
    </g>

    <!-- 3. camera vision -->
    <g>
      <text x="440" y="86" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#f0b429"/>
      <text x="440" y="86" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#f0b429">Camera vision</text>
      <rect x="440" y="96" width="176" height="104" rx="8" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--border-2)"/>
      <path d="M456 178 L456 116 L600 116 L600 178 Z" fill="rgba(240,180,41,0.08)" stroke="#f0b429" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <circle cx="528" cy="152" r="9" fill="#f0b429"/>
      <path d="M528 152 L488 128 L568 128 Z" fill="rgba(240,180,41,0.18)" stroke="#f0b429" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      <text x="440" y="222" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">Needs: daylight and a lawn</text>
      <text x="440" y="238" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">edge it can actually see.</text>
      <text x="440" y="254" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">Fails when: dusk, long grass</text>
      <text x="440" y="270" font-size="11" fill="#c9c9d1">meeting long grass.</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="note">
    Wire-free is two quite different technologies sold under one phrase. Which one suits you is
    decided by your garden — tree cover rules out satellite, a soft lawn edge is hard for vision —
    rather than by which is newer.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .dgm { margin: 1.75rem 0; }
  .dgm svg { max-width: 640px; display: block; }
  .dgm .note { margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
